            <ArticleTitle>A randomised trial comparing the H Pipelle with the standard Pipelle for endometrial sampling at 'no-touch' (vaginoscopic) hysteroscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1471-0528.2008.01992.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate the effectiveness and tolerance of H Pipelle compared with the standard Pipelle as an endometrial biopsy device at outpatient 'no-touch' hysteroscopy.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">A prospective randomised trial carried out in an outpatient diagnostic hysteroscopy clinic.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">A large undergraduate teaching hospital.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="POPULATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Sixty women investigated for abnormal menstruation in an outpatient diagnostic hysteroscopy clinic.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Prospective randomised trial comparing the H Pipelle with the standard Pipelle de Cornier.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES" NlmCategory="METHODS">Adequacy of the biopsy specimens and women's experience.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Ninety-three percent (H Pipelle) and 87% (Pipelle) of the biopsy specimens were judged to be adequate for histological diagnosis (P &gt; 0.05). However, obtaining endometrial sampling with the H Pipelle was significantly quicker (median times: 39 seconds [H Pipelle] and 102 seconds [Pipelle], P &lt; 0.0001) and less painful (median visual analogue scale score: 1 [H Pipelle] and 5 [Pipelle], P = 0.011).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The H Pipelle not only makes it possible to perform hysteroscopy and endometrial biopsy with minimal instrumentation but is also associated with a shorter biopsy time and less discomfort than the standard Pipelle without any loss of biopsy adequacy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
